From: Chris <chris.dixon.78.burnbridge@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Stop opening an EGL display the core does not own

Two places call eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY) whenever EGL is defined,
which is every GLES build. There is no default display to open on a GBM
system, so both fail:

  EGL Debugging:
  Error: EGL_BAD_ALLOC
  Command: eglGetDisplay
  Message: EGL_BAD_ALLOC error: In eglGetPlatformDisplay: Failed to create
           EGLDisplay

Neither call is needed under libretro, where the frontend creates and owns the
context and hands the core its framebuffer and get_proc_address.

DisplayWindowMupen64plus::_start() calls eglInitialize() on that display and
throws the result away -- it is not stored, not checked, and nothing else in
the file touches EGL. Its only purpose was to initialise a display the core
does not own.

isEGLExtensionSupported() sets one thing, GLInfo::eglImage, and the only code
that acts on it is guarded by EGL and OS_ANDROID together:

  ColorBufferReader * ContextImpl::createColorBufferReader(CachedTexture *_pTexture)
  {
  #if defined(EGL) && defined(OS_ANDROID)
      if (m_glInfo.eglImage)
          return new ColorBufferReaderWithEGLImage(...);
  #endif

as is ColorBufferReaderWithEGLImage itself. So off Android the probe can only
fail, and the flag it sets feeds nothing that is compiled. Give it the same
guard as its consumer.

Non-Android EGL builds keep every colour buffer reader they had -- the EGLImage
one was never among them -- and stop opening a display they have no use for.

--- a/GLideN64/src/Graphics/OpenGLContext/mupen64plus/mupen64plus_DisplayWindow.cpp
+++ b/GLideN64/src/Graphics/OpenGLContext/mupen64plus/mupen64plus_DisplayWindow.cpp
@@ -76,10 +76,6 @@
 	_getDisplaySize();
 	_setBufferSize();

-#ifdef EGL
-	eglInitialize(eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY), nullptr, nullptr);
-#endif // EGL
-
 	LOG(LOG_VERBOSE, "[GlideN64]: Create setting videomode %dx%d", m_screenWidth, m_screenHeight);
 	return true;
 }
--- a/GLideN64/src/Graphics/OpenGLContext/opengl_Utils.cpp
+++ b/GLideN64/src/Graphics/OpenGLContext/opengl_Utils.cpp
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@

 bool Utils::isEGLExtensionSupported(const char * extension)
 {
-#ifdef EGL
+#if defined(EGL) && defined(OS_ANDROID)
 	const char* where = strchr(extension, ' ');
 	if (where || *extension == '\0')
 		return false;
